  "limitations": [
    "The 88-case feature sample now retains 20 failures and is not a compatibility percentage. A passing probe does not establish whole-feature compatibility.",
    "Table-level/composite REFERENCES, deferred constraints, CASCADE/SET NULL/SET DEFAULT/RESTRICT actions, foreign_key_check/list pragmas and cross-table ALTER rename handling retain limitations. Unadmitted action syntax is rejected by certified grammar.",
    "The supported parent lookup uses existing scalar affinity and BINARY comparison. Other declared collations remain unsupported.",
    "The source-free CREATE write-text relation excludes unretained REFERENCES declarations. Cache equality, private row-effect database preservation, the transition predicate and in-transaction flag no-op have audited component contracts. These do not prove whole-SQL equivalence, all foreign-key semantics, physical storage refinement or crash behavior.",
    "Existing UTF-16, views/triggers, STRICT, WITHOUT ROWID, expression/partial index and other SQL/storage limitations remain. The 60 SIGKILL cases exercise earlier storage paths rather than every foreign-key schedule."
  ],
